I am using the `cloud` models for an agent (OpenClaw), and I've noticed that these models are subject to session and weekly limits. Currently, the only way to monitor these limits is through the web UI.

I would like a way to query this usage data via the API so that agents can programmatically monitor their remaining quota and adjust their behavior (e.g., switching to a local model when cloud limits are nearly reached) to avoid abrupt interruptions.

**Proposed Endpoint:** `GET /api/usage` (or similar)

**Example Response:**
```json
{
  "session_usage": {
    "percentage": 5.1,
    "resets_in": "5 hours"
  },
  "weekly_usage": {
    "percentage": 50.3,
    "resets_in": "4 days"
  },
  "model_distribution": {
    "gemma4:31b-cloud": 60,
[... log trimmed ...]
```

<img width="559" height="294" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/78430f0c-154f-4299-b9cf-06481787471d" />

Providing this data via the API would greatly improve the developer experience for anyone building automated workflows or agents using Ollama's cloud infrastructure.

